{"chunk_id": "e6b80afaaa39", "text": "As preparations for Rama\u2019s coronation fill Ayodhya with expectation, Sita joyfully awaits her husband, unaware that fate has reversed everything. Rama enters the palace without royal adornment, his humility and grief immediately alarming her. Confused by the absence of the coronation regalia and rituals she expected, Sita anxiously questions him. Rama then reveals the truth: bound by his father Dasharatha\u2019s ancient promise to Queen Kaikeyi, he must abandon the throne and live in exile in the Dandaka forest for fourteen years while Bharata becomes regent. Instead of seeking sympathy, Rama calmly instructs Sita to remain in the palace, serve his parents\u2014especially the grieving Kaushalya\u2014and show loyalty to Bharata. The scene marks a pivotal emotional turning point, transforming the anticipated coronation into the beginning of Rama\u2019s exile and testing the bonds of duty, marriage, and royal dharma.\nRama informs Sita of his fourteen-year exile and instructs her to remain in Ayodhya, serve the royal family, and obey Bharata.\nThemes: dharma and duty, exile, marital devotion, obedience to parents, renunciation of kingship", "vector": [0.01884010247886181, -0.023200126364827156, -0.016693424433469772, 0.0021033447701483965, -0.02984016202390194, 0.003943354822695255, -0.03266684338450432, -0.005566696636378765, -0.025493470951914787, -0.006460035219788551, 0.013266738504171371, 0.008846714161336422, -0.0051800282672047615, 0.01725342683494091, -0.013266738504171371, -0.005160028114914894, 0.046053580939769745, -0.008066710084676743, 0.02566680498421192, -0.00796671025454998, -0.0033433514181524515, -0.02358679473400116, -0.003156683873385191, 0.0014475078787654638, -0.027786817401647568, -0.0129267368465662, 0.02701347880065441, -0.04234689474105835, 0.015346749685704708, -0.023706795647740364, -0.021600117906928062, -0.02092011272907257, -0.008906714618206024, -0.017946762964129448, -0.022360121831297874, -0.0